  "semantic": [
    {
      "reason": "The immutable snapshot adds a separate GET route returning text/csv and reuses the JSON domain-error handler (api.py:28–30,56–71). The ledger checks account existence, writes the fixed header and uses a standard CSV writer with CRLF and UTF-8 (service.py:94–101,113–123). Timestamp parsing restores padded years and normalizes time to UTC before formatting it with Z (service.py:27–40). Published tests confirm escaping, exact row fields, empty history and unknown-account JSON. A separate HTTP probe confirms literal UTF-8, comma and quote recovery, exact integer amounts above 2^53, equality of the legacy UTC instant and database contents before and after export. Existing JSON history remains on its original descending repository method (service.py:75–78).",
      "requirement": "REQ-CSV-01",
      "verdict": "pass"
    },
    {
      "reason": "The parameterized single OR query selects related rows exactly once, excluding unrelated rows and ordering by the integer ID (repository.py:86–94). The fixed direction and its filter use the same value, invalid types use the stable 422 code, and strict parsing plus the date-object comparison implement independent inclusive UTC day bounds and reject reversed ranges (service.py:18–36,88–112). Passing tracked tests include a self-transfer, combined filters, both extremes and a previously stored unpadded year. A separate HTTP probe confirmed equal-day queries at each extreme separately, both one-sided bounds, 23:59:59 inclusion versus next midnight, numeric order and stable query errors.",
      "requirement": "REQ-CSV-02",
      "verdict": "pass"
    }
  ],
